.env
.env.local
.env.*
# The two lines above correctly keep real secrets (.env, infra/.env, any
# .env.local) out of git -- but .env.* also matched .env.example and
# infra/.env.example, the two template files README.md's "Getting
# started" tells a fresh clone to copy from. Neither file was ever
# actually in the repository because of this: `git log --all` has zero
# commits touching either path. Un-ignore them explicitly.
!.env.example
!infra/.env.example
node_modules/

# Go build cache (used for sandboxed builds)
.gocache/
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store
